---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ContactPerson } from "../components/ContactPerson";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>For contractors | Spokane List</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Free Spokane-area listings so a neighbor can paste your complete name—not a screenshot—in a group chat. No account, no lead fee."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">For contractors</p>
    <h1>When a neighbor shares you, they paste something complete</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Free listing. No account. No lead fee. This exists so a recommendation in
      a Facebook group or neighborhood chat actually reaches your phone.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Most of your work already comes from word of mouth. Someone asks for a
        plumber. A neighbor drops your name from memory. Then the pile-on: what’s
        the number, do they have a site, what’s their Google? The person who
        meant to help goes hunting. You never get the call.
      </p>
      <p>
        A listing here is a paste-ready packet: name, trade, city, rating, phone,
        site, and a link that still works in the group. The recommendation
        travels complete. That is the point—more of those warm mentions turn into
        a ring, not another profile for you to manage.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why you should want this</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>You sit in the channel that already feeds your phone.</strong>{" "}
          A neighbor paste beats a cold search result. The homeowner is already
          asking who to hire.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Free. No account. No bidding for the same job.</strong> You
          don’t pay a lead fee to stay listed, and you don’t log in to keep it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No second profile.</strong> Keep your{" "}
          <a href="https://business.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Google Business Profile
          </a>{" "}
          current. We refresh from that—not a Yelp-style page you maintain here.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The share is your sales sheet.</strong> Rating and review count
          travel with the name. License can sit on the page. They are not
          depending on a screenshot of Maps.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <p>
        This does not replace Google, and it does not guarantee jobs. Volume is
        still neighborhood word of mouth. The win is cleaner, more complete
        referrals with no extra work.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What the free listing does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A shareable page with your name, trade, city, phone, and site.</li>
        <li>Google rating and review count when we have them.</li>
        <li>A listing link that holds up when someone pastes it in a group.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Keep your{" "}
        <a href="https://business.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          Google Business Profile
        </a>{" "}
        current, then <a href="/get-listed">request a listing</a> or a fix. We
        refresh from GBP—we don’t run a second profile you have to manage here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you ever want a hand</h2>
      <p>
        Some local contractors ask for help getting more Google reviews, cleaning
        up a Business Profile, or putting up a simple website that matches this
        listing. If that’s useful, you’re welcome to write. If not, the directory
        stays free either way.
      </p>
      <ContactPerson />
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/get-listed">Request a listing</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/">See the directory</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
